  "summary_en": "Textbook chapter introducing ethical design considerations for robotics. It covers normative ethical theories, the non-neutrality of technology, value-sensitive design, stakeholder identification, ethics checklists, standards and frameworks, and the AIRR responsible innovation framework, using a medical delivery drone crash as a motivating case.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Technology is not ethically neutral and exists in a context.",
   "Robot designers should apply value-sensitive design and identify impacted stakeholders.",
   "Ethics checklists, standards and design frameworks help embed ethics, though self-administered checklists have limits.",
   "The AIRR framework supports responsible innovation in robotics.",
   "Designers must ask whether a robot should be built at all."
  ],
